. 
. *-----------------------------------------------
. * Compute Cronbach's alpha and create scale
. *-----------------------------------------------
. //This part of the code is for internal consistency of our analysis. You can 
> comment out this part if necessary.
. //Support for gender equality attitudes
. alpha plh0357 rc_plh0298 rc_plh0302 plh0308_v2 plh0359 plh0360

Test scale = mean(unstandardized items)

Average interitem covariance:     1.299632
Number of items in the scale:            6
Scale reliability coefficient:      0.7314

. // It turned out that Cronbach's Alpha value for our six-item scale is 0.75.
. // We, therefore, retain all the items for our mean attitude score. 
. 
. *compute the respondent's mean gender attitude scores
. gen attitude_mean = (plh0357 + rc_plh0298 + rc_plh0302 + plh0308_v2 + plh0359
>  + plh0360) / 6

. 
. 
. *-----------------------------------------------
. * Treatment and moderator variables
. *-----------------------------------------------
. 
. * Has at least one daughter
. gen has_daughter = 0

. foreach var of varlist kidsex01-kidsex15 {
  2.     replace has_daughter = 1 if `var' == 2
  3. }
